			<div class="content" id="post-content-3260244">
									

<p>Protip: Always google something you're unfamiliar or unsure about.</p>
<p>An Arming Sword is the technical name of what most people nowadays would call a longsword. One handed, simple crossguard, blade between 28-31 inches (70-80&#160;cm). They are also known as <a href="https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knightly_sword">Knightly Swords</a>.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">To be fair, though, the sword in question would likely be simply called a &quot;<a href="https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viking_sword">Viking Age Sword</a>&quot; or Carolingian Sword.</span></p>
<p>Nevermind. It's dated to a transitional period between Carolingian and Knightly Swords, where neither terms would be a perfect fit.</p>

